                                "id": "8d7a6973-401e-4429-9b83-53fd0cbd0f46",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) Amplitude. Since both sound waves have the same pitch, their frequency and wavelength must be the same. According to the relationship between frequency, amplitude, and wavelength, if the amplitude increases, the wave becomes louder. Therefore, the second sound wave must have a greater amplitude to be louder than the first sound wave.",
                                "answer_from_choices": null,
                                "correct_answer": null
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/03/30 05:23:30",
