                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Identify the sources of energy available in the tank.\n2. Determine which source(s) the crickets could have used for energy.\n3. Eliminate sources that are unlikely to have provided all of the crickets' energy.\n4. Choose the source that is most likely to have provided all of the crickets' energy.\n\nAnswer:\n1. The sources of energy available in the tank are sunlight, water, soil, and plants.\n2. Crickets are not able to directly use sunlight or water for energy. They could have used the plants or the soil as a source of energy.\n3. It is unlikely that the crickets gained all of their energy from the soil, as soil does not contain enough nutrients to sustain them. Therefore, we can eliminate option A.\n4. The crickets likely gained all of their energy from the plants, as they are herbivores and feed on plant material. Therefore, the correct answer is C) the plants.",
