                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What was the source of energy for the crickets kept in a classroom tank with sunlight, water, soil, and plants?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- Crickets need energy to survive.\n- The tank had sunlight, water, soil, and plants.\n- Sunlight provides energy through photosynthesis in plants.\n- Plants use energy from sunlight to produce glucose through photosynthesis.\n- Glucose is a source of energy for living organisms.\n- The crickets had access to plants in the tank.\n- Therefore, the crickets gained all of their energy from the plants in the tank.\n\nAnswer: C) the plants.",
