                        "cot": "B) a learned behavior.\n\nThis is a classic example of classical conditioning, where the bird associates the bright color of the insect with the bad taste and learns to avoid it in the future. It is not a physical characteristic, as it does not involve any changes to the bird's body. It is not an inherited behavior, as it is not passed down genetically from the bird's parents. It is not necessarily an adaptation, as it may not directly improve the bird's chances of survival, but rather a learned response to a specific stimulus.",
