                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What is the definition of \"the passage of genetic instructions from one generation to the next?\"\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- A) Growth: Growth refers to the process of increasing in size or number, but it does not necessarily involve the passing of genetic instructions from one generation to the next.\n- B) Heredity: Heredity is the passing of traits from parents to offspring through genes, which involves the passage of genetic instructions from one generation to the next. This seems to be the correct answer.\n- C) Development: Development refers to the process of maturing or progressing through stages, but it does not necessarily involve the passing of genetic instructions from one generation to the next.\n- D) Reproduction: Reproduction is the process of producing offspring, which involves the passing of genetic instructions from one generation to the next. However, reproduction is not the only way genetic instructions can be passed down, as heredity can also occur through other means such as cloning or genetic engineering.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) heredity.",
