                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The passing of genetic instructions from one generation to the next is a fundamental concept in biology and is known as heredity. It involves the transmission of genetic information from parents to offspring through the process of reproduction.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is heredity?\n2. What is the process of reproduction?\n3. How is genetic information transmitted from parents to offspring?\n\nAnswering the sub-questions:\n1. Heredity is the passing of genetic instructions from one generation to the next.\n2. Reproduction is the process by which organisms produce offspring.\n3. Genetic information is transmitted from parents to offspring through the DNA molecules that make up the chromosomes in the cells of the parents. During reproduction, the genetic information is passed on to the offspring through the fusion of gametes (sperm and egg cells) from the parents.\n\nAnswer to the original question:\nB) Heredity is defined as \"the passage of genetic instructions from one generation to the next.\"",
