                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Determine the genotype of the parent guinea pigs.\n2. Use a Punnett square to determine the possible genotypes and phenotypes of their offspring.\n3. Calculate the probability of each phenotype.\n\nAnswer:\n1. The parent guinea pigs are both black (Bb), meaning they each carry one dominant black allele (B) and one recessive white allele (b).\n2. Using a Punnett square, we can determine the possible genotypes and phenotypes of their offspring:\n   | B  | b  |\n---|---|---|\nB  | BB | Bb |\nb  | Bb | bb |\n   The possible genotypes are BB, Bb, and bb.\n   The possible phenotypes are black (BB and Bb) and white (bb).\n3. The probability of each phenotype can be calculated by counting the number of times it appears in the Punnett square. \n   The probability of black fur is 3/4 or 75% (BB, Bb, Bb).\n   The probability of white fur is 1/4 or 25% (bb).\nTherefore, the answer is D) 75% black, 25% white.",
