                    {
                        "id": "3086c82f-9bb4-4c68-85a9-2a452280a73a",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: In genetics, dominant traits are expressed when an individual has at least one copy of the dominant allele, while recessive traits are only expressed when an individual has two copies of the recessive allele.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are the possible genotypes of the two black guinea pigs?\n- Each black guinea pig must have at least one dominant B allele, so their genotypes could be BB or Bb.\n2. What are the possible gametes (sperm and egg cells) that each black guinea pig can produce?\n- A BB guinea pig can only produce B gametes, while a Bb guinea pig can produce both B and b gametes.\n3. What are the possible genotypes of the offspring?\n- The offspring can inherit one allele from each parent, so the possible genotypes are BB, Bb, or bb.\n4. What are the possible phenotypes (observable traits) of the offspring?\n- BB and Bb genotypes will both result in black fur, while bb will result in white fur.\n\nAnswering the sub-questions:\n1. The genotypes of the two black guinea pigs could be BB or Bb.\n2. A BB guinea pig can only produce B gametes, while a Bb guinea pig can produce both B and b gametes.\n3. The possible genotypes of the offspring are BB, Bb, or bb.\n4. BB and Bb genotypes will both result in black fur, while bb will result in white fur.\n\nAnswer: \nSince both parent guinea pigs are Bb, they can each produce both B and b gametes. When these gametes combine to form offspring, there are three possible genotypes: BB, Bb, or bb. BB and Bb genotypes will both result in black fur, while bb will result in white fur. Therefore, the offspring can be either black or white, but since both parents are black, at least one of the offspring must be black. The possible ratios of black to white offspring are 3:1 or 75% black and 25% white. Therefore, the answer is D) 75% black, 25% white.",
                        "answers": [
