                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: An indicator is a substance that changes color in the presence of an acid or a base. Vinegar is an acid, and ammonia solution is a base.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is an indicator?\n2. What is vinegar?\n3. What is ammonia solution?\n4. What happens when an acid and a base are mixed together?\n\nAnswers:\n1. An indicator is a substance that changes color in the presence of an acid or a base.\n2. Vinegar is an acid.\n3. Ammonia solution is a base.\n4. When an acid and a base are mixed together, they undergo a neutralization reaction, which results in the formation of water and a salt. In this case, the ammonia solution neutralized the vinegar, causing the color to disappear. Therefore, the process that occurred was D) neutralization.",
