                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nProtons and neutrons are about the same size, but neutrons are a bit heavier. So, we can say that one proton plus one neutron is roughly the same as two protons.\n\nElectrons are much smaller than protons and neutrons, so we can say that one proton plus one electron is roughly the same as two protons.\n\nSo, if we add the number of protons to the number of electrons, we get the number of nucleons (protons and neutrons).\n\nNow, if we subtract the number of protons from the number of neutrons, we get the number of neutrons.\n\nSo, the mass of an atom is calculated by subtracting the number of protons from the number of neutrons.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
