                    {
                        "id": "e8659fa4-182e-425d-9bc2-72acbb65748e",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, let's review the different states of matter and their transitions:\n\n- Solid: particles are tightly packed and vibrate in place\n- Liquid: particles are close together but can move past each other\n- Gas: particles are far apart and move freely\n\nTransitions between these states can occur through changes in temperature and pressure. For example:\n\n- Melting: solid to liquid\n- Freezing: liquid to solid\n- Vaporization: liquid to gas\n- Condensation: gas to liquid\n- Sublimation: solid to gas\n- Deposition: gas to solid\n\nNow, let's consider the question. We are asked what could occur as a result of decreasing the heat energy of a gas. Heat energy is a form of energy that is transferred from one object to another due to a difference in temperature. When we decrease the heat energy of a gas, we are essentially cooling it down.\n\nBased on our knowledge of the different states of matter and their transitions, we can eliminate options C (radiation) and D (vaporization) as they do not involve a change from gas to another state.\n\nOption B (evaporation) is also unlikely, as evaporation typically occurs when a liquid is heated and its particles gain enough energy to escape into the air as a gas. Decreasing the heat energy of a gas would not cause it to evaporate.\n\nTherefore, the most likely answer is A (condensation). When we cool down a gas, its particles lose energy and move closer together. If we continue to cool it down, the gas will eventually reach its dew point, which is the temperature at which it begins to condense into a liquid. This is why we see condensation on a cold glass of water or on the outside of a can of soda on a hot day.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "6bf6712d-a301-48f0-a5b9-c0961b64c493",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "A) condensation.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "A",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
