                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What is a possible outcome of reducing the heat energy of a gas?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- When heat energy is decreased, the particles in the gas will have less kinetic energy and move more slowly.\n- This could cause the gas to lose energy and potentially change state.\n- Condensation and vaporization are both changes in state that involve the transfer of heat energy.\n- Evaporation and radiation are not changes in state, but rather processes that can occur within a particular state.\n- Therefore, the possible outcome of decreasing the heat energy of a gas is condensation (option A) or vaporization (option D).\n\nAnswer: A) condensation or D) vaporization.",
