                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Heat energy is the energy that is transferred from one body to another as a result of a difference in temperature. Gas is a state of matter that has no fixed shape or volume and can be compressed or expanded.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What happens to gas when heat energy is decreased?\n2. What are the different states of matter?\n3. What is condensation?\n4. What is evaporation?\n5. What is radiation?\n6. What is vaporization?\n\nAnswers:\n1. When heat energy is decreased, the gas molecules lose energy and move slower, causing the gas to contract and decrease in volume.\n2. The different states of matter are solid, liquid, gas, and plasma.\n3. Condensation is the process by which a gas or vapor changes into a liquid.\n4. Evaporation is the process by which a liquid changes into a gas or vapor.\n5. Radiation is the emission of energy as electromagnetic waves or as moving subatomic particles, especially high-energy particles that cause ionization.\n6. Vaporization is the process by which a liquid or solid changes into a gas or vapor.\n\nAnswer: A) Condensation could occur as a result of decreasing the heat energy of a gas.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "7a6eafde-48b4-4144-9c5e-9dc44a745994",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "A) condensation. When the heat energy of a gas is decreased, the gas molecules lose energy and move slower, causing the gas to contract and decrease in volume. This can lead to the gas molecules coming closer together and forming a liquid, which is the process of condensation.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "A",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/03/30 05:30:53",
