                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-17",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain the question again, please?\n\nProfessor: Sure. The question is asking what could happen to a gas if its heat energy is decreased.\n\nStudent: Okay, got it. So, what are the options?\n\nProfessor: The options are condensation, evaporation, radiation, and vaporization.\n\nStudent: Can you explain what each of those means?\n\nProfessor: Sure. Condensation is when a gas turns into a liquid. Evaporation is when a liquid turns into a gas. Radiation is the emission of energy as electromagnetic waves or as moving subatomic particles. And vaporization is when a liquid turns into a gas.\n\nStudent: Okay, I think I understand. So, which one of these options could occur if the heat energy of a gas is decreased?\n\nProfessor: Well, if the heat energy of a gas is decreased, it means that the gas is losing energy. And if a gas loses energy, it will tend to condense into a liquid. So, the answer is A) condensation.\n\nStudent: Oh, I see. Thank you for explaining that to me.",
