                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nWater, ice, and steam are all different states of the same substance, which is water. The temperature of a substance depends on the amount of heat energy it contains. When heat energy is added to a substance, its temperature increases, and when heat energy is removed, its temperature decreases.\n\nIce is the solid state of water, and it has the lowest temperature of the three. This is because the molecules in ice are tightly packed together, and they have very little kinetic energy. Therefore, ice is the coldest of the three.\n\nWater is the liquid state of water, and it has a higher temperature than ice. This is because the molecules in water have more kinetic energy than those in ice, and they are able to move around more freely. Therefore, water is warmer than ice.\n\nSteam is the gaseous state of water, and it has the highest temperature of the three. This is because the molecules in steam have the most kinetic energy, and they are moving around very rapidly. Therefore, steam is the hottest of the three.\n\nBased on this reasoning, the correct order from coldest to hottest is A) ice, water, steam.",
