                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step-by-step procedure:\n1. Research the melting and boiling points of water, ice, and steam.\n2. Determine which state of matter has the lowest melting point (coldest temperature) and which has the highest boiling point (hottest temperature).\n3. Arrange the states of matter in order from lowest melting point to highest boiling point.\n\nGoing through each step:\n1. The melting point of ice is 0\u00b0C and the boiling point of water is 100\u00b0C. The boiling point of steam is 100\u00b0C as well.\n2. Ice has the lowest melting point, making it the coldest. Steam and water have the same boiling point, but steam is hotter because it requires more energy to reach that point.\n3. The order from coldest to hottest is therefore: A) ice, water, steam.",
