                        "cot": "The correct answer is D) keeping food fresh.\n\nHelpful knowledge: Refrigerators are appliances that use electricity to cool and preserve food. They work by removing heat from the interior of the fridge and expelling it to the outside.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the purpose of refrigerators?\n2. How do refrigerators work?\n3. What happens to food when it is not kept cold?\n4. How does refrigeration help keep food fresh?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The purpose of refrigerators is to keep food cold and preserve it for longer periods of time.\n2. Refrigerators work by using electricity to remove heat from the interior of the fridge and expelling it to the outside. This process cools the air inside the fridge and helps to preserve the food.\n3. When food is not kept cold, it can spoil quickly due to the growth of bacteria and other microorganisms. This can lead to foodborne illnesses and food waste.\n4. Refrigeration helps keep food fresh by slowing down the growth of bacteria and other microorganisms that cause food to spoil. By keeping food at a low temperature, refrigerators help to preserve the quality and safety of food for longer periods of time.",
