                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Astronomy has been studied for thousands of years and has been used for various purposes, including navigation and timekeeping.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. How did people use the stars to navigate ships?\n2. Did people use the stars to study the weather?\n3. Is there a connection between the stars and volcanic eruptions?\n4. How did people use the stars to map the Earth's surface?\n\nAnswers:\n1. People used the stars to navigate ships by observing the position of certain stars in the sky and using them as reference points to determine their location and direction.\n2. While people did not use the stars to study the weather directly, they did use astronomical observations to create calendars and predict seasonal changes, which could indirectly help with weather forecasting.\n3. There is no direct connection between the stars and volcanic eruptions, but some ancient cultures believed that certain celestial events, such as eclipses, could be omens of impending disasters like volcanic eruptions.\n4. People used the stars to map the Earth's surface by creating celestial maps that showed the positions of stars and constellations in the sky. These maps could be used to navigate and explore new territories.",
