                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: In a Cartesian coordinate system, the vertical axis is typically labeled as the y-axis and represents the dependent variable.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is a dependent variable?\n2. What is an independent variable?\n3. What is the purpose of a graph?\n4. What types of data are typically plotted on a graph?\n\nAnswers:\n1. A dependent variable is a variable that is being measured or observed and is affected by the independent variable.\n2. An independent variable is a variable that is being manipulated or changed in an experiment or study.\n3. The purpose of a graph is to visually represent data and relationships between variables.\n4. The types of data that are typically plotted on a graph include numerical data, such as measurements or counts, and categorical data, such as types or categories.\n\nAnswer: C) Dependent variables are most likely placed along the y-axis.",
                        "answers": [
